values ('bbbb0002-0000-4000-8000-000000000038', 'en', null, 'Quantum Computing', 'Quantum computing explained from the ground up - qubits, superposition, entanglement, gates, and the famous algorithms - with the math kept conceptual and every piece of notation written in plain ASCII. Each reading builds intuition first, then grounds it in worked examples and quick self-checks, and the course closes on hardware, error correction, and the real-world impact on cryptography. Structure and reference material adapted from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 43, true, 'technology', '{}')
